{
  "title": "Use YAML front matter for metadata",
  "template": "madr",
  "decided_on": null,
  "status_raw": null,
  "status": null,
  "decision_makers": [],
  "consulted": [],
  "informed": [],
  "extra": {
    "nav_order": 13,
    "parent": "Decisions"
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "kind": "context",
      "raw_heading": "Context and Problem Statement",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "parent": null,
      "text": "\nMADR offers the fields \"Status\", \"Decision Maker(s)\", and \"Date\".\nThese are a kind of metadata fields.\nShould this data be included in the ADR directly, or should it be separated somehow?\n\n",
      "option_key": null,
      "byte_start": 78,
      "byte_end": 301
    },
    {
      "kind": "drivers",
      "raw_heading": "Decision Drivers",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "parent": null,
      "text": "\n* Easy to read\n* Easy to write\n\n",
      "option_key": null,
      "byte_start": 301,
      "byte_end": 354
    },
    {
      "kind": "options",
      "raw_heading": "Considered Options",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "parent": null,
      "text": "\n* Use YAML front matter\n* Use plain Markdown everywhere\n\n",
      "option_key": null,
      "byte_start": 354,
      "byte_end": 434
    },
    {
      "kind": "outcome",
      "raw_heading": "Decision Outcome",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "parent": null,
      "text": "\nChosen option: \"Use YAML front matter\", because comes out best (see below).\n\n",
      "option_key": null,
      "byte_start": 434,
      "byte_end": 532
    },
    {
      "kind": "pros_cons",
      "raw_heading": "Pros and Cons of the Options",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "parent": null,
      "text": "\n",
      "option_key": null,
      "byte_start": 532,
      "byte_end": 565
    },
    {
      "kind": "pros_cons",
      "raw_heading": "Use YAML front matter",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "parent": 4,
      "text": "\nExample:\n\n```markdown\n---\nstatus: accepted\ndecision-makers:\ndate:\n---\n\n### Context and problem statement\n\nWe want to record architectural decisions made in this project.\nWhich format and structure should these records follow?\n```\n\nRendered output:\n\n![adr-013 rendered output](0013-example.png)\n\n* Good, because it shortens the body (essence of the ADR)\n* Good, because tools can handle it more easily\n* Good, because indicates the lower importance of the data\n* Bad, because pretends to be more accurate than it can be (e.g., possible status values)\n* Bad, because rendering not standardized\n* Bad, because not all Markdown parsers can parse it\n\n",
      "option_key": "opt:use yaml front matter",
      "byte_start": 565,
      "byte_end": 1238
    },
    {
      "kind": "pros_cons",
      "raw_heading": "Use plain Markdown everywhere",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "parent": 4,
      "text": "\n* Good, because all parsers can handle it\n* Bad, because special markdown parsing tooling is needed\n* Bad, because metadata is handled the same way as the content\n\n",
      "option_key": "opt:use plain markdown everywhere",
      "byte_start": 1238,
      "byte_end": 1437
    },
    {
      "kind": "more_info",
      "raw_heading": "More Information",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "parent": null,
      "text": "\n[ADR-0008](0008-add-status-field.md) reasons on adding metadata (such as status).\n",
      "option_key": null,
      "byte_start": 1437,
      "byte_end": 1540
    }
  ],
